    "blurb": "The show erupts with a monster Truckin' → The Other One stretch and a blistering Big River. Jerry’s tone is hot all night, Phil adds depth on the extended jam, and the rhythm section stays tight throughout.",
    "review": "September 17, 1972 finds the Dead in top form at the Baltimore Civic Center, delivering one of those rare high‑energy outings that still feels fresh decades later. The first set rolls through classics—Bird Song, Big River, and a seamless China Cat → I Know You Rider transition—setting an eager tone, while the second set launches into a marathon Truckin' → The Other One that stretches the improvisational muscles to their limits. Jerry charges out on Truckin', his Strat singing with a hot, searing lead before diving deep into an unrelenting Other One where Phil’s bass crumbles in just‑the‑right places and Bill adds extra beats that hint at his 1973 style. The climax arrives with a soaring Sing Me Back Home solo that feels both cowboy‑spirit and transcendent, followed by a crisp Sugar Magnolia that caps the set. An encore of One More Saturday Night rounds out an evening where every member is locked in, making this Baltimore show a standout entry in the ’72 catalog.",
